WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.190
Picture a booming economy.

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:04.770
Shops are busy, firms are hiring,

3
00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.310
and job adverts are everywhere.

4
00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:10.220
Yet unemployment never falls to zero.

5
00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.570
And when a recession hits,

6
00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:13.130
it can soar.

7
00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:16.320
In the United States,
unemployment rose from 5 per cent

8
00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:20.490
to 10 per cent between 2007 and 2009.

9
00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:22.850
So why are some people out of work even

10
00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.900
when the economy is booming?

11
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.080
In this mission, you'll meet the
different types of unemployment

12
00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:30.030
and what causes each one.

13
00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.020
Then you'll count the costs:

14
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:36.150
for people, for communities
and for the whole economy.

15
00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.090
Your mission: find out
why there are always some

16
00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:42.030
people out of work, even
in the best of times.
